  "featStitch": "Merge long screenshots",
  "featStitchBody": "Join a scrolling capture back into one tall image, with the overlap found and removed automatically.",
  "featUnlimited": "Unlimited screenshots",
  "featUnlimitedBody": "The free tier organizes {count} screenshots and keeps {folders} folders. Pro takes both numbers away.",
  "featUnlimitedBodyPro": "Your library has no ceiling — keep as much as you like.",
  "featSafeShareHow": "Finding what is private in a screenshot is free and unlimited. Paying is what turns those findings into a clean copy: each detail you leave selected is covered in the exported image, which is flat — no layer to undo.",
  "featSafeSharePoint1": "Card numbers are Luhn-checked and IBANs mod-97 checked, so those two are found by proof rather than by pattern — no guessing on the detail that matters most.",
  "featSafeSharePoint2": "Also catches names, addresses, order numbers, verification codes, phone numbers and email addresses.",
  "featSafeSharePoint3": "You see everything found before you send, and can leave any of it showing if the app got it wrong. The original screenshot is never touched.",
  "featActionsHow": "Whatever is written inside a screenshot becomes something you can use. Shoto picks out the useful parts and puts a button on each one.",
  "featActionsPoint1": "Links, email addresses, IBANs, verification codes, dates and parcel numbers are found for you.",
  "featActionsPoint2": "One tap to open or copy — no reading characters off a picture.",
  "featActionsPoint3": "Works on the screenshots you already have, not only on new ones.",
  "featTraitsHow": "Filtering is free on whatever Shoto has already read: search, smart actions and Safe share each leave recognised text behind, and every filter is derived from that. Paying is what reads the rest of the library in one pass, so a filter can also see the screenshots no other feature has opened yet.",
  "featTraitsPoint1": "Five filters — card numbers and IBANs, links, phone numbers and email addresses, verification codes, and dates you are expected to turn up for.",
  "featTraitsPoint2": "Card numbers and IBANs are proven by checksum. The rest are read from the picture, so they under-report rather than over-claim.",
  "featTraitsPoint3": "The library always says how many screenshots have never been read, so an empty result is never passed off as an absence. Reading happens on the phone; nothing is uploaded.",
  "featTint": "Choose your accent",
  "featTintBody": "{count} accents for the buttons, switches and selections — each one tuned to stay readable in both light and dark.",
  "@featTintBody": {
    "placeholders": {
      "count": {
        "type": "int"
      }
    }
  },
  "featTintHow": "Most apps hand you a row of raw colours and let the contrast fall where it may, which is why a yellow accent usually arrives carrying white text nobody can read. Shoto stores your choice as a position on the colour wheel rather than as a fixed colour, then works out the exact shade for light mode and for dark mode — so whichever you pick carries text at the same strength the app's own colour does.",
  "featTintPoint1": "{count} accents, from teal and moss through amber and ember to plum, indigo and slate.",
  "@featTintPoint1": {
    "placeholders": {
      "count": {
        "type": "int"
      }
    }
  },
  "featTintPoint2": "Each one is worked out twice, once for light mode and once for dark, against the same contrast target — so no accent glows on a dark screen or disappears on a pale one.",
  "featTintPoint3": "Red for delete, green for done and amber for warnings never change, so a colour that means something never becomes decoration.",
  "featStitchHow": "Scrolling capture, on a phone that has it, has to be started while you are still on the page. Shoto works afterwards: pick two or more shots already in your library — including ones somebody sent you — and it finds where they overlap and joins them into one tall image.",
  "featStitchPoint1": "The repeated strip between two shots is found and removed automatically.",
  "featStitchPoint2": "You see the join before anything is saved — automatic detection is good, but never certain.",
  "featStitchPoint3": "The merged image saves to your gallery like any other picture.",
  "featDuplicatesHow": "Sharing shots in one at a time rarely makes duplicates. Keeping a batch from \"Since you last looked\" does — you move fast, and two captures of the same thing both get kept. Shoto compares by what a shot looks like, not its name or size, so it catches those, along with a resend or a different crop.",
  "featDuplicatesPoint1": "Groups whatever looks the same and suggests the copy worth keeping.",
  "featDuplicatesPoint2": "Shows how much space each group frees before you decide anything.",
  "featDuplicatesPoint3": "Nothing is deleted until you have reviewed the group and confirmed it.",
  "featUnlimitedHow": "The free tier is a real, usable app: saving, folders, favourites and full search, with no account and nothing uploaded. It has two ceilings — how many screenshots it organizes, and how many folders it keeps — and Pro removes both. Everything you already organized stays exactly where it is.",
  "featUnlimitedPoint1": "The free tier keeps {count} folders, which is exactly the starter set Shoto gives you. Pro takes that number away too.",
  "featUnlimitedPoint2": "Naming what a screenshot is for is free and uncapped too.",
  "featUnlimitedPoint3": "Hitting the ceiling means Shoto became where you keep things. Nothing is deleted when you do.",
